 "title": "MAX4080/MAX4081: 76 V high-side current-sense amplifiers, voltage out, gain 5, 20 or 60 V/V",
 "source": {
  "document": "19-2562",
  "revision": "Rev 6, 12/20",
  "pages": 14
 },
 "summary": "High-side current-sense amplifiers that read the drop across an external shunt sitting on a rail anywhere from 4.5 V to 76 V and give a voltage output. The supply, also 4.5 V to 76 V, is independent of the sensed rail. The MAX4080 senses one direction with a ground-referred output; the MAX4081 senses both, its output centred on a voltage set at two reference pins. Each comes in three fixed gains (5, 20, 60 V/V), in 8-pin µMAX or SO, for -40 °C to +125 °C.",
 "key_figures": [
